<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 1: GLOBAL OVERVIEW
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section" id="s1">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-number">1</div>
    <div class="section-title">Global Homicide Rate Overview</div>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>This section presents the overarching trajectory of intentional homicide rates across {total_countries} countries and territories, as reported to the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC) between 1990 and 2023. The data reveal a broad, long-term decline in homicide rates at the global level — but this narrative of improvement is uneven and requires careful contextual interpretation.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-title">Global Median & Mean Homicide Rates Over Time</div>
    <div class="card-subtitle">Rates per 100,000 population. The median is more robust to extreme outliers; divergence between mean and median signals skew from high-rate countries.</div>
    <div class="chart-container">
      <canvas id="globalTrendChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-title">Reporting Countries Over Time</div>
      <div class="chart-container">
        <canvas id="coverageChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-title">Decade-over-Decade Trajectory</div>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Period</th><th class="num">Mean Rate</th><th class="num">Change</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1990s</td><td class="num">{fmt(mean_90s)}</td><td class="num">—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2000s</td><td class="num">{fmt(mean_00s)}</td><td class="num"><span class="trend-indicator" style="color:{trend_color(change_90s_00s)}">{pct_fmt(change_90s_00s)} {trend_arrow(change_90s_00s)}</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>2010s</td><td class="num">{fmt(mean_10s)}</td><td class="num"><span class="trend-indicator" style="color:{trend_color(change_00s_10s)}">{pct_fmt(change_00s_10s)} {trend_arrow(change_00s_10s)}</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>2020s (partial)</td><td class="num">{fmt(mean_20s)}</td><td class="num"><span class="trend-indicator" style="color:{trend_color(change_10s_20s)}">{pct_fmt(change_10s_20s)} {trend_arrow(change_10s_20s)}</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="callout callout-info" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <strong>Key finding:</strong> The global mean homicide rate has moved from {fmt(mean_90s)} per 100k in the 1990s to {fmt(mean_20s)} in the 2020s. While the overall direction is {'downward' if (mean_20s or 0) < (mean_90s or 999) else 'mixed'}, the pace of decline has {'slowed' if change_10s_20s and abs(change_10s_20s) < abs(change_00s_10s or 0) else 'varied across decades'}.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight-box">
    <h4>Analytical Note</h4>
    <p>Interpreting global trends requires caution: the set of reporting countries changes each year. Early years (1990s) have fewer reporting countries, which may skew global aggregates. The "improvement" narrative partly reflects improved data coverage from lower-rate nations joining the reporting pool. Section 6 discusses these limitations in detail.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 2: REGIONAL & COUNTRY COMPARISON
